message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "triptych: a Prolog realisation of Sun, a system poem"
abstract: >-
  A Prolog realisation of the system poem Sun. A ten-word grid of nouns,
  verbs, adverbs and the deictic now generates seventy-two variants
  through fixed combinatory constraints — three nouns by three verbs by
  four adverbs by two syntactic orders. The seventy-two variants are
  mapped onto the seventy-two eclipses of Saros 126 (1179–2459). The
  language is chosen for its declarative architecture, which states the
  constraints of the system rather than the steps to execute them, after
  the glossematics of Louis Hjelmslev.
